| `make test-fe-unit` `[local]` | Runs each frontend app's unit runner, its npm script `test:unit` (Vitest in the shipped stacks), over the app's own modules; a runner that finds no test fails, so a stack cannot pass with zero tests. | `make test-fe-unit` | [`FE_APPS`](settings.md#make-variables) | Exits 0 with no output when no frontend app is found. Exits 2, before any app runs, when `npm` or `node` is not on `PATH` or an app lacks `node_modules/.package-lock.json`, npm's completion marker, naming the app and `make fe-install`: a suite that ran nothing does not pass. Red on zero tests or an app without the `test:unit` script. Not for the browser: `make test-fe-e2e`. | [dev-loops.md](../guides/dev-loops.md) | always |
